@@ -0,0 +1,165 @@
+# cua-macos-visual provenance
+
+Fixed upstream revision: `2d2f99228d4d2508dc6fcc84c176b296e146714a`
+
+Fixed upstream source root: `libs/cua-driver/rust`
+
+This crate is a functional subset, not an ABI-equivalent replacement for the
+R7 SDK graph. It owns one observation's window facts, pixels and conversion
+checks only. It does not own submissions, leases, frame publication, input
+dispatch, AX semantics, screen recording, clipboard, overlay/PiP, browser or
+daemon lifecycle.
+
+## Source mapping
+
+### `crates/platform-macos/src/windows.rs` -> `src/window.rs`
+
+Kept:
+
+- `CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo` restricted to on-screen, non-desktop-element
+  windows (`kCGWindowListOptionOnScreenOnly |
+  kCGWindowListExcludeDesktopElements`).
+- Optional reads of `kCGWindowNumber`, `kCGWindowOwnerPID`, `kCGWindowLayer`
+  and all four `kCGWindowBounds` components.
+- Pure checked parsing (`RawWindowFact` -> `WindowIdentity`): missing keys,
+  non-finite values, non-positive sizes, non-layer-0 windows and values that do
+  not fit `u32`/`i32` are rejected. Nothing is defaulted to `0` or truncated.
+
+Removed:
+
+- `kCGWindowOwnerName`, `kCGWindowName`, z-index, on-screen and Space fields.
+- SkyLight Space queries, AX reachability filtering and helper-window pruning.
+- All public window enumeration and selection helpers. The remaining reader is
+  `pub(crate)` and only reachable from the crate-private capture path.
+
+Not supported this round: off-Space, minimized and accessory/overlay windows.
+Because enumeration is on-screen only, an absent window is `WindowNotFound`, not
+a silently accepted zero fact. A request with a non-zero layer is rejected.
+
+### `crates/platform-macos/src/capture.rs` -> `src/capture.rs` + `src/observe.rs`
+
+Kept:
+
+- `SCShareableContent::get()` and selection of the one exact requested window.
+- Desktop-independent `SCContentFilter` built with `with_window`.
+- `point_pixel_scale` / `content_rect` output sizing, rounded and bounded.
+- `SCStreamConfiguration` with `shows_cursor(false)`.
+- `SCScreenshotManager::capture_image`.
+- CGImage dimension/RGBA length checks.
+- Identity revalidation before capture, against the selected SCK window and
+  after the frame is returned. Drift is rejected; the window is never reselected.
+
+Added pure orchestration:
+
+- `observe_once` takes injected before/select/capture/after/encode closures and
+  enforces the order. Tests prove drift stops later stages, a bad RGBA length
+  stops before the after-check, an after-drift stops before encoding, and no
+  empty PNG can become a successful frame. The native path calls this same
+  function, so the tested order is the order actually used.
+
+Removed:
+
+- The two-second plan cache, native capture gate, worker timeout, retry after
+  identity change, shell `screencapture` fallback and SkyLight fallback.
+- `capture_consent`, display capture, overlay exclusion, video recording,
+  recording hooks and all input/pointer/overlay/PiP dependencies.
+
+Not solved here:
+
+- `SCScreenshotManager::capture_image` ends in a one-shot
+  `SyncCompletion::wait()` inside `screencapturekit 8.0.1`; if the system never
+  invokes the callback, this synchronous call can stay pending indefinitely.
+  This candidate deliberately adds no fake timeout or cancellation.
+- CGWindow PID/window/geometry agreement is observation consistency only. It is
+  not process-incarnation proof, foreground authorization, a lease or a
+  published final frame.
+
+### `crates/cua-driver-core/src/image_utils.rs` -> `src/png.rs`
+
+Kept:
+
+- `encode_rgba_to_png`, now using `PngEncoder` directly from the caller's slice
+  with no `rgba.to_vec()` clone.
+- `png_dimensions` as an explicitly header-only IHDR parser.
+
+Added:
+
+- `verify_png_matches_dimensions` first bounds the input length and walks the
+  chunk container with checked lengths. It verifies every chunk CRC, requires
+  IHDR first, at least one IDAT and a final zero-length IEND, and rejects any
+  trailing bytes. `image` then performs only the bounded pixel decode. This
+  rejects a 24-byte IHDR-only fake, truncation (including a missing IEND), a bad
+  IEND or other chunk CRC, trailing garbage, non-RGBA8 colour type, wrong pixel
+  byte count and aggregate pixel/RGBA budget overflow before a success frame can
+  be formed.
+- Aggregate pixel/RGBA budget checks (`MAX_CAPTURE_PIXELS`, `MAX_RGBA_BYTES`)
+  in addition to the per-side limit.
+
+Removed:
+
+- JPEG encoding, PNG-to-JPEG conversion, resizing, crosshair drawing and
+  BGRA conversion.
+- The workspace `image` feature set. This crate depends on `image 0.25` with
+  `default-features = false, features = ["png"]`, so JPEG encoding is not
+  compiled through this crate's direct dependency.
+
+### `crates/platform-macos/src/tools/px_frame.rs` -> `src/geometry.rs`
+
+Kept:
+
+- `validate_capture_frame`'s coherent 1x/2x scale rule and refusal on zero or
+  non-finite bounds.
+
+Removed:
+
+- `WindowPxFrame::to_screen`. It has no validated caller in this round, and an
+  unchecked public pixel-to-screen transform would accept NaN/infinity or a
+  zero scale. It is not carried as a public API.
+- `ToolResult` refusal JSON, `error_structured`, `resolve_or_refuse` and the
+  native `resolve_window_px_frame` convenience. This crate exposes only pure
+  geometry; a frame is not wired to action dispatch.
+
+## Dependency and platform notes
+
+- `screencapturekit = 8.0.1` with `features = ["macos_14_2"]`.
+  `default = []`; `macos_14_2` enables `macos_14_0`, which enables `macos_13_0`.
+  `macos_14_2` is the minimum feature that exposes `SCContentFilter::content_rect`
+  (the method is `#[cfg(feature = "macos_14_2")]` in 8.0.1). The capture plan
+  still uses `SCScreenshotManager` and `point_pixel_scale` from `macos_14_0`.
+- The dependency's `build.rs` always configures and builds the Swift bridge and
+  links multiple Apple frameworks. Enabling only `macos_14_0` does not remove
+  the recording Swift sources from the dependency build, and this crate does not
+  claim that the upstream SCK library contains no recording code. Raising the
+  feature floor to `macos_14_2` likewise does not remove those sources.
+- The existing R7 SDK/platform crates keep their own `macos_15_0` selection;
+  this crate does not change those old candidates.
+- `build.rs` is a new, crate-local link-path helper. It runs only the absolute
+  `/usr/bin/xcrun --find swiftc`, requires one absolute
+  `<toolchain>/usr/bin/swiftc` result, verifies that compiler file, derives the
+  same toolchain's `usr/lib/swift/macosx`, and verifies that both
+  `libswiftCompatibility56.a` and `libswiftCompatibilityPacks.a` exist. Only
+  then does it emit `cargo:rustc-link-search=native=...`. It also emits
+  `cargo:rustc-link-arg=-Wl,-rpath,/usr/lib/swift` for this crate's test/final
+  executable, because upstream Swift objects reference the system Swift runtime
+  through `@rpath` and the compatibility-library search path alone does not
+  satisfy runtime loading. This is the standard system runtime directory; the
+  script does not set `DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH`, copy a library, disable validation,
+  force-link unrelated frameworks, modify a registry/global SDK setting, or
+  lower the deployment target. The Swift object files keep their own autolink
+  directives. It has no `DEVELOPER_DIR`, `xcode-select`, or hard-coded global
+  fallback: xcrun failure, a relative/multi-line/wrong-layout result, or a
+  missing library fails the build. An `rlib` does not carry this runtime
+  closure: a future Helper consumer must put the same rpath on its own final
+  executable. The existing minimum-deployment warnings for upstream Swift
+  objects are not resolved by this helper.
+- No cache, lease, registry migration, shell, SkyLight, AX SPI or TCC request is
+  introduced.
+
+## License
+
+- `LICENSE-MIT` is a verbatim copy of the fixed upstream root `LICENSE.md` at
+  `2d2f99228d4d2508dc6fcc84c176b296e146714a`, SHA-256
+  `c0779290c1d4783169aa3dbfb55feb505e563ef8a004bbf55298ceffcfbda8d9`,
+  1069 bytes. It is not a template.
+- The crate expression is the workspace `MIT`; the copied text is the actual
+  copyright/license body from the fixed upstream object.
